```python
def card_status(task_id):
    for pat in (os.path.join(WORK, task_id, "longrun", "results", "*.md"),
                os.path.join(ROOT, "results", task_id.replace("_", "-") + ".md")):
        for c in glob.glob(pat):
            txt = open(c, errors="ignore").read()
            tail = txt[-400:]
            if "TASK_BLOCKED" in tail:
                return "blocked", c
            if "TASK_DONE" in tail:
                return "done", c
    return None, None
```

glob order is arbitrary (filesystem order). It iterates over all .md files in longrun/results and returns "done" if any has TASK_DONE in its tail. The card path returned may be D6-weekly-release.md if it comes first and has TASK_DONE. Let me check D6-weekly-release.md tail. Either way, it returns done as long as some card has TASK_DONE in the tail. Since the D8 card has TASK_DONE at the end, we're fine.

